{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:QOU.Knot.GradedGeneratingFunction"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.gf_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.gf_pow","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BodyOrderExpansion.lean#L180-L193","doc":"**The `A`-fold form: `G_1(x)^A`.** Over `A` independent copies of one block,\nwith the total degree the sum of the blocks' degrees and the coefficient their\nproduct, the generating function is the single block's raised to the `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.gf_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.gf_product","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BodyOrderExpansion.lean#L168-L178","doc":"**The generating function is multiplicative over a product index set**,\nwhen the degree is additive and the coefficient multiplicative across the\nfactors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.body_eq_graded_of_bond_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.body_eq_graded_of_bond_product","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BodyOrderExpansion.lean#L129-L142","doc":"**The field, discharged.** `QOU.Mass.BodyOrderJetGrading.body_eq_graded`\nasserts `bodyTerm n = gradedTerm n`. In the bond-product model\n`bodyTerm n = Σ_{|t| = n} ∏_{e ∈ t} d_e` (the `n`-body cluster sum) and\n`gradedTerm n` is the coefficient at grade `|s| - n`, given by\n`prod_bonds_graded`. `esymm_eq_compl_sum` is exactly the equation between them.\n\nSo the assumed field is a theorem here, and it is not definitional: the two\nsides are different expressions over different index sets, related by the\ncomplement bijection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.esymm_eq_compl_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.esymm_eq_compl_sum","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BodyOrderExpansion.lean#L106-L127","doc":"**The complement bijection.** Summing each `n`-subset's product equals\nsumming, over `(|s| - n)`-subsets, the product over the complement. This is\nwhat makes the body index and the grade index two readings of one grading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.prod_bonds_bot_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.prod_bonds_bot_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BodyOrderExpansion.lean#L79-L83","doc":"The all-bodies end: the `X ^ 0` coefficient is the product of every bond\nscalar -- the single `|s|`-body term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.prod_bonds_top_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.prod_bonds_top_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BodyOrderExpansion.lean#L72-L77","doc":"The `0`-body end: the top grade `X ^ |s|` carries coefficient `1`, since the\nonly subset of size `|s|` is `s` itself and its complement is empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.prod_bonds_graded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.prod_bonds_graded","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BodyOrderExpansion.lean#L58-L70","doc":"**Body order = filtration grade.** Regrouping the expansion by how many\nbonds contribute an `X`, the coefficient of `X ^ k` is the sum over all\n`(|s| - k)`-subsets of bonds of the product of their scalars -- i.e. the\n`(|s| - k)`-body term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.prod_bonds_expand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.BodyOrderExpansion.prod_bonds_expand","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/BodyOrderExpansion.lean#L49-L56","doc":"**The bond product, expanded over subsets.** Each bond contributes either\nits `X` (to `t`) or its scalar (to the complement). ","signatureChunk":0}]}